{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). In this decision problem, Lottery A offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, so it has a sure outcome. Lottery B offers 1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability, so it does not have a sure outcome. The decision reason prefers the lottery *without* a sure outcome, which is Lottery B. Thus, the reason would lead to a preference for Lottery B over Lottery A. The relevant information (presence or absence of a sure outcome) is clearly derivable from the problem.",
